NEXERATH — HARMONIC HARVEST LATTICE
BEKW-CODE Open Hardware · Engineering Save State v0.2
THE 77 / CANDIDATE #04  
Design status: Concept architecture + buildable test plan; not a performance-certified product  
Design lineage: NEXERATH × G.E.R.A.L.D. restorative-material pipeline  
Doctrine: Art with a job. The landfill becomes the cathedral.  
Release intent: Open technical collaboration; choose final licensing and attribution before public distribution.
> **Prime statement:** NEXERATH is a family of kinetic, visibly functioning sculptures fabricated from documented reclaimed materials. Its modules intercept real ambient energy flows—temperature differences, sunlight, airflow, vibration, water motion, and deliberate human interaction—convert portions of those flows into electricity, combine intermittent outputs through a low-loss harvest lattice, and spend the accumulated energy on useful work. Each installation is a unique, repairable archive of the place from which its materials were recovered.
Founding distinction: NEXERATH is neither a perpetual-motion claim nor a disposable art object. It has identifiable external energy inputs, a measurable electrical output, a persistent material provenance record, and a functional job. Custom components, tools, molds, alloys, and fabrication methods are first-class design options.
---
1. The invention, kept whole
NEXERATH performs six functions concurrently:
Harvest: collect available gradients and motion using multiple independent transducers.
Aggregate: condition otherwise incompatible trickles, pulses, voltages, and waveforms onto a common energy-storage architecture.
Work: power a real low-energy service—an environmental observation node, timed signal, civic information display, or local telemetry device.
Remember: retain and display the history of recovered components, including old working parts and visible relics.
Teach: expose mechanisms, measurements, and cause-and-effect directly to visitors.
Restore: turn materials recovered by G.E.R.A.L.D. into durable public or domestic assets.
The aspiration is a visible scientific cathedral: blown, cast, or reclaimed glass; copper and brass; rhythmic magnet shuttles; slow vanes; spring reeds; illuminated charge paths; the occasional historical component embedded where it can be admired and, where appropriate, still function.
What counts as success
A successful NEXERATH is beautiful, instrumented, honest about its inputs, repairable, and demonstrably powered by harvested energy over a specified operating interval. Yield need not be enormous. Measured useful work, material recovery, and educational merit together justify the machine.
The distinctive engineering opportunity
Many individual harvester technologies already exist. NEXERATH's innovation target is their materially diverse, low-loss aggregation inside a uniquely reclaimed, openly documented kinetic sculpture whose power budget and salvage provenance are publicly intelligible.
