7. First build: NEXERATH-B0, the truth rig
Purpose: demonstrate at least one genuine ambient-to-electric conversion, then combine three source classes onto one monitored storage system. Build a gorgeous exposed demonstration without prematurely making any subsystem untouchable or inaccessible for testing.
Proposed footprint
Parameter	Starting choice	Reason
Total height	600 mm	Desktop-scale gallery apparatus
Base	250 × 250 mm, weighted	Stable, serviceable frame
Visible chimney	400–500 mm height, approx. 70–100 mm inner diameter	Removable convection experiment
Thermal chamber	Approx. 50–150 mL test displacement volume	Initial stroke/pressure characterization, not a certified pressure-vessel specification
Reed arm	100–200 mm adjustable	Allows resonance tuning
Magnet-coil cartridge	One removable winding and shuttle fixture	Shared manufacturing method
Electrical bus	3 input channels plus optional direct PV/TEG	Proves aggregation rather than a single decorative trick
Storage	Instrumented supercap test module	Reveals small charge events without hiding them in a large battery
Control	Duty-cycled logger/display, optionally powered from isolated test supply during characterization	Prevents measurement overhead masking harvested results
Mechanical construction sequence
Survey salvage stock. Photograph each candidate, remove unsuitable/hazardous parts, assign provisional IDs.
Make the holding jig. A 250-mm-base fixture with slots and a removable vertical spine provides repeatable test geometry.
Wind a generator cartridge. Establish wire gauge/turn-count options; record DC resistance and response to a known magnet stroke.
Prove one source. Begin with controlled vibration or repeatable thermal transients and capture energy into a local capacitor.
Build the thermal motion demonstration. Instrument actual gradient/displacement; progress toward repeatable cycle and an induction output.
Build and tune the convection chimney. Characterize flow and turbine drag with heat source and cold sink conditions recorded.
Connect three sources through independent front ends. Verify no cross-discharge, stable startup and independent contribution.
Add the sculpture. Reclaimed glass, readable copper, protective transparent panels, historical placards and measured-energy lighting.
Demonstrate the job. Use stored energy to perform a named service, e.g. one temperature/humidity sample and saved timestamp at an adjustable interval.
Publish numbers and the provenance ledger. Include failed runs, configuration changes, and what each source contributed.
Proposed fabrication fixtures and tools
Custom coil winder and mandrels; magnet shuttle alignment fixture.
Adjustable reed/tuning jig with marked masses.
Rotor balancing fixture and detachable turbine blade pitch templates.
Thermal interface/diaphragm clamp and non-destructive leak-testing arrangement.
Separate electrical instrumentation board with current sense and guarded test points.
Mechanical guards for spinning parts and an accessible emergency electrical isolation method.
